  "interpretation": "For these paired cases, updating the connector is sufficient to reproduce the visible degradation even with the original DiT. Keeping the aligned connector with the adapted DiT largely preserves the pre-joint scene. The factorial flow gaps and original-norm feature drift support connector-side loss of alignment as the primary measured effect. This does not isolate prefix vs content contributions within the connector or establish all future DiT training is safe.",
  "limits": [
    "Four distinct matched captions total: two train and two held out. Three timesteps per caption are correlated probes; six observations per split are not six independent examples.",
    "Only two generated cases, one matched seed each. These local counterfactuals identify causes for these examples, not population-wide performance.",
    "Caption gap is a controlled denoising sensitivity metric, not caption or image-generation accuracy. All routes win all six small-cohort comparisons despite visible PRISM subject failures.",
    "The original aligned baseline already missed important subjects. Avoiding additional degradation does not establish readiness for full-data training.",
    "Prefix MSE grows about twentyfold from a small baseline, but content and suffix also drift; this experiment does not show that prefix alone causes generation degradation.",
    "Checkpoint bytes were independently hashed remotely and strict restores executed on Aurora. This local audit verified archived evidence and sources without transferring or loading checkpoint tensors."
  ],
  "recommendation": {
    "full_data_training_supported": false,
    "next_bounded_hypothesis": "Retain the verified region-aligned connector behavior during joint updates, e.g. compare a lower connector learning rate or an explicitly recorded alignment-retention objective, then repeat matched-noise subject checks and caption controls. A frozen-connector DiT-only route can serve as a control, but its six-update counterfactual still lacks full subject recovery. Broader caption alignment from the prepared pool remains a separate hypothesis for the original held-out failures."
  },
